# PART 1 — PRODUCT FOUNDATION

## 1.1 Product vision

Udta Teer's website will be an interactive digital representation of Jaipur, designed to communicate the agency's creative, technical and marketing capabilities through an immersive city-based storytelling experience.

The visitor should not experience the website as a collection of disconnected sections. Instead, they should feel as though they are travelling through a digital version of Jaipur.

During this journey:

- The city introduces the brand.
- The arrow guides the visitor.
- Different establishments introduce services.
- Business locations introduce industry-specific solutions.
- Project showcases demonstrate execution capabilities.
- A structured journey explains how Udta Teer works.
- The final destination introduces the project planner.

The entire experience should have a consistent narrative.

## 1.2 Business objectives

The website must fulfil the following objectives.

### Objective A — Brand differentiation

Create a recognisable identity that differentiates Udta Teer from conventional agencies.

Success conditions:
- Jaipur should be recognisable through architecture, colours and environmental elements.
- The arrow should become a recognisable brand interaction.
- The website should communicate a modern agency rather than a tourism business.
- The brand should feel credible to both small businesses and established organisations.

### Objective B — Service discovery

Visitors should understand what Udta Teer offers without navigating through complicated menus.

Success conditions:
- Three primary service pillars are immediately understandable.
- Every pillar has a detailed service breakdown.
- Every service explains its business value.
- Visitors can navigate directly to relevant services.

### Objective C — Industry-wide customer acquisition

Udta Teer should serve businesses across different industries through requirement-specific solutions.

Potential customer segments:
- Retail and jewellery.
- Restaurants and cafes.
- Hospitality and tourism.
- Education and institutions.
- Healthcare and professional services.
- Real estate and construction.
- Handicrafts and lifestyle.
- Startups and SaaS.
- Manufacturing and industrial businesses.
- D2C and e-commerce brands.
- Local service providers.
- Other small, medium and enterprise businesses.

These are target segments, not claims about existing clients.

### Objective D — Flexible commercial model

The service and pricing architecture should accommodate both smaller businesses and more complex requirements.

Commercial direction:
- Public starting price: ₹2,999.
- Requirement-specific packages.
- Custom combinations of design, development and marketing.
- One-time project pricing.
- Monthly recurring service plans where applicable.
- Custom quotations for complex requirements.

The ₹2,999 starting price must not imply that every service or complete solution is available at that amount.

### Objective E — Lead generation

Every important section should provide an opportunity to initiate a project discussion.

Primary conversion actions:
- Build My Growth Plan.
- Take Your First Shot.
- Request a Quote.
- Book a Consultation.
- Request a Free Audit.
- Chat on WhatsApp.

### Objective F — Long-term scalability

The website should support the addition of:
- New services.
- New industry pages.
- New portfolio projects.
- New pricing packages.
- Blog articles.
- Landing pages.
- Additional marketing campaigns.

The content architecture should allow these additions without rebuilding the entire website.

